From abd297b3fe2b1f93f24b2c9037b84cc010e604e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:18:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Book meetings automatically: Meet link email + admin calendar
 event

Converse already detected when a prospect wants to meet (the
"meeting_request" outcome in agents/converse/policy.py) but nothing acted
on it beyond moving the funnel stage. This wires up the missing half:

- integrations/calendar.py: creates a Google Calendar event with an
  auto-generated Meet link on the admin's calendar (service account +
  domain-wide delegation). Falls back to a stub Meet link when
  GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON isn't set, so the app still runs out of the
  box, matching this repo's existing dev-fallback pattern.
- integrations/mailer.py: emails the participant that Meet link plus a
  reminder of when the meeting is. Falls back to logging the email when
  SMTP isn't configured.
- orchestrator/meeting_scheduler.py: picks a default slot, resolves which
  admin's calendar to use (env override -> ADMIN-role user -> campaign
  owner), and ties the two integrations together. Wired into
  orchestrator/service.py's process_converse for the "advance_meeting"
  action.
- CampaignProspectLink gains meeting_link/meeting_scheduled_at/
  calendar_event_id (model + table + mapper + Alembic migration) so the
  booking is visible wherever the link already is.
- backend/.env.example documents the new (and existing) env vars.
- backend/tests/test_meeting_scheduler.py covers the dev-fallback paths
  and the default-slot calculation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
